## What to deliver

Build and rig the fortress up operation by operation until each `parts/<part>.png`
matches the brief, the assembled `scene/` previews show the parts fitting together
correctly, and the rig is complete: a heavily armored citadel raised on legs, carrying
a big main turret and forward cannon, a side-mounted turret out on each flank, and a
sweeping radar vane — all as a smooth, rounded, watertight Surface Nets surface. **Author
the three required animations** as F-curves with the `sn-anim` animation subcommands:
`march` (a walk whose feet plant flat and still, then lift and swing — with weight, not
a weightless slide), `bombardment` (the guns working while the fortress stands), and
the self-playing `radar_spin`. The animations are the fixed contract — produce all
three, by those names; the parts and joints that realize them are yours. When you are
satisfied, stop: the emitted per-part meshes and `rig.json` are your finished
submission.
